            <abstract>
                <p>Longinus is a name given in the apocryphal literature to the unnamed Roman soldier from
                    the Gospels who pierced a side of Jesus with his lance. He is believed to be one
                    of the first Roman converts to Christianity and is considered a saint in the Roman
                    Catholic, the Ethiopian Orthodox and some other Churches. He often appears in miniatures.</p>
            </abstract>
